    "answer_seconds": 10.007995013002073,
    "total_seconds": 10.394600315004936,
    "answer": "Based on ACME policies, the following requirements and protections apply:\n\n* **Privileged Access Controls (Information Security Policy):** Privileged access (admin/root) requires Multi-Factor Authentication (MFA). All access must be individual and auditable (shared or generic accounts are prohibited) and is subject to quarterly review and recertification.\n* **Device and Remote Security (Information Security Policy & Acceptable Use Policy):** Laptops must have full-disk encryption enabled (BitLocker for Windows or FileVault for Mac). Data in transit must use TLS 1.2 or higher, and data at rest must be encrypted with AES-256. Circumventing security controls (such as VPN bypass or disabling endpoint protection) and storing sensitive data on personal devices are strictly prohibited.\n* **Remote Work Conditions (Remote Work Policy):** The administrator must maintain core hours of 10:00 AM \u2013 3:00 PM local time, respond on Slack within 30 minutes during core hours, and maintain a safe, ergonomic workspace. Working remotely up to 3 days per week requires completing a 6-month probationary period and manager agreement; 5 days per week requires VP approval; and working outside the country of employment requires written approval from HR and Legal.",
